"""SYSTEM-MANIFEST-1 (Rowan, 2026-11-25): "There must be a standard easy way to do this ... standards that can apply these things broadly and
can synchronize across multiple surfaces and providers." Ultrastable is the foundation for any autonomous system.

One manifest per system (`ultrastable.json` at the repository root, its `identity` object validated by standards/system.schema.json) and one
reconciler: every surface that says what the system is and where it runs is rendered from the manifest, never typed per surface. Each rendered
file follows its own published standard; the copyright holder is read from LICENSE (its "Licensor:" line), never guessed.

  python3 scripts/surfaces.py --check  [--root DIR]         the manifest is valid, a copy no longer claims the template, and every surface equals
                                                            what the manifest renders (exit 1 on drift)
  python3 scripts/surfaces.py --render [--root DIR]         write every surface: README blocks (identity, Live, How this system runs), publiccode.yml,
                                                            catalog-info.yaml (Backstage), CITATION.cff fields, llms.txt, REUSE.toml, LICENSES/<id>.txt,
                                                            codemeta.json, .ultrastable/github.json; and CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md
                                                            only when they are missing (people and loops add to those); a surface that waits
                                                            on a fact the repository lacks (its holder, a long enough description) is named,
                                                            the rest are written, and the command exits 1 while one waits
  python3 scripts/surfaces.py --adopt [--repo OWNER/NAME] [--name NAME] [--summary TEXT] [--public-url URL] [--root DIR]
                                                            a copy of the template takes its own identity (the repository is read from IDEA.md,
                                                            the Action's own checkout or the git remote when not given) and renders every surface
  python3 scripts/surfaces.py --plan [github|wellknown|publiccode|all] [--root DIR]   print the provider payloads; nothing is called
  python3 scripts/surfaces.py --validate [--root DIR]       the manifest against the schema only

Pure standard library; carried by every system. Platform wrapper: `python3 -m foundation surfaces`. Tests: tests/test_surfaces.py."""
